00:00:10.640 --> 00:00:11.440
[Laughter]

00:00:14.800 --> 00:00:17.360
Niko: Hey guys, welcome back to another episode of Stuntmen React

00:00:17.440 --> 00:00:21.980
Niko: We're happy to be able to finally film with guests again and Gui has graciously come in

00:00:21.980 --> 00:00:24.080
Niko:  Gui is a legend, he's done some incredible things

00:00:24.080 --> 00:00:30.200
Niko: He's going to give you that professional insight into one of the most unique and coolest jobs that you could ever possibly have

00:00:30.200 --> 00:00:32.040
Clint: So yeah, we're gonna hop into some clips here

00:00:32.040 --> 00:00:36.040
Clint: Let's get started with one of my favorite Kung fu movies of all time

00:00:38.960 --> 00:00:42.860
Clint: Kung Fu Hustle is directed by one of my all-time favorite directors

00:00:42.860 --> 00:00:45.280
Clint:  I could go on for hours about how much I love Stephen Chow

00:00:45.440 --> 00:00:47.060
Gui: I love his versatility
Clint: Same

00:00:47.060 --> 00:00:49.060
Gui: Definitely one of my favorite directors of all time

00:00:49.060 --> 00:00:50.560
Clint: He is a genius

00:00:51.180 --> 00:00:53.920
[Yelling]

00:00:56.800 --> 00:00:57.860
Clint: So good

00:00:59.440 --> 00:01:01.600
Gui: So he's in... he's on a Hong Kong harness

00:01:01.840 --> 00:01:06.060
Gui: Which only... it's like a belt and it goes through... it's similar to what climbing harness looks like

00:01:06.060 --> 00:01:06.560
Clint: Okay

00:01:06.720 --> 00:01:09.680
Gui: He's picked at the hips, so that when he jumps

00:01:10.080 --> 00:01:13.519
Gui: They... they time it with him and doesn't lift up his shirt or anything like that

00:01:13.600 --> 00:01:16.739
Gui: What I really like about the Hong Kong harness is the fact that it allows

00:01:17.200 --> 00:01:22.060
Gui: Your athleticism to be part of the performance rather than you just going for the ride

00:01:22.160 --> 00:01:25.280
Clint: Yeah
Gui: In a sense, which they need him to do at this moment because he has to

00:01:25.520 --> 00:01:30.000
Gui: Be in rhythm with them and bounce and jump at the same time and throw the kicks and land

00:01:30.560 --> 00:01:32.799
Gui: And have that weight on top of it

00:01:36.480 --> 00:01:38.740
Niko: Kicks them so hard dust comes off of them

00:01:38.740 --> 00:01:40.000
Niko: They need to wash their clothes some more

00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:40.860
Clint: Wait a second

00:01:40.960 --> 00:01:44.500
Clint: How'd they get that dust puff, on that face kick right here?

00:01:44.500 --> 00:01:45.000
Clint:  Look at this

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:46.420
Gui: Yeah
Clint: Did he throw it with his hand?

00:01:46.600 --> 00:01:47.100
Gui: No

00:01:47.440 --> 00:01:48.240
Gui: It's on his foot

00:01:48.240 --> 00:01:49.460
Niko: It just flicks off his toe

00:01:49.700 --> 00:01:54.880
Niko: Also in a little bit later you can see there's a part where he just slides his foot through a pile to kick it up into the air, also

00:01:54.880 --> 00:01:56.000
Niko: Gui, what do you use for that dust?

00:01:56.000 --> 00:02:01.420
Gui: I mean usually you use baby powder, but there is another kind of dust that's a little bit thicker, that we use

00:02:04.960 --> 00:02:06.960
Niko: You just slam his head on the ground

00:02:07.360 --> 00:02:08.959
Niko: Nope
Gui: No, he didn't he saved himself
Clint: That was a shoulder or something

00:02:08.960 --> 00:02:09.760
Gui: That was great

00:02:09.760 --> 00:02:11.400
Gui: That was actually a really good reaction

00:02:11.400 --> 00:02:12.260
Clint: He got caught

00:02:12.320 --> 00:02:13.980
Gui: Pow! look he used his arm to save himself

00:02:13.980 --> 00:02:14.740
Clint: He was like, "Boom!"

00:02:14.740 --> 00:02:15.540
Gui: Just enough

00:02:15.540 --> 00:02:17.220
Gui: Just... just... just enough

00:02:21.440 --> 00:02:22.780
Clint: Dude that enough got launched

00:02:22.780 --> 00:02:26.220
Clint: Look at this guy... roller coaster ride

00:02:32.160 --> 00:02:34.000
Niko: That's so rad such a sick reveal

00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:35.380
Gui: well this part's cg, right

00:02:35.380 --> 00:02:37.780
Clint: That's real
Gui: This is real and then he goes

00:02:37.780 --> 00:02:38.280
[Metal clinking]

00:02:38.480 --> 00:02:39.680
Gui: Absolutely VFX

00:02:39.940 --> 00:02:42.100
Gui: And then this is just glued together

00:02:46.300 --> 00:02:47.640
Gui: I believe it's Hung Ga

00:02:48.040 --> 00:02:51.060
Gui: It's a northern style, so it's very deep stances

00:02:51.060 --> 00:02:56.120
Gui: The style tiger that you see in kung fu films for the most part is of that origin

00:02:56.160 --> 00:02:58.620
Gui: Which also will explain why a lot of the...

00:02:58.960 --> 00:03:02.740
Gui: Martial arts movements of this style is it's always so big and round

00:03:02.740 --> 00:03:07.060
Gui: Because they're actually hitting with their forearms more than their fists at times

00:03:12.480 --> 00:03:16.240
Clint: Dude that move
Gui: Yeah, that double the jump split back kicks

00:03:17.600 --> 00:03:20.740
Clint: He does a really good job of making impossible moves look possible

00:03:20.740 --> 00:03:23.220
Gui: Right, He's very anime inspired

00:03:23.360 --> 00:03:23.840
Clint: Yeah

00:03:23.840 --> 00:03:27.040
Gui: That's what I really liked about Kung Fu Hustle and resonated with me

00:03:27.040 --> 00:03:32.700
Gui: Was his ability to take ideas from animation and put it into live action

00:03:32.700 --> 00:03:33.420
Clint: Dude, 100%

00:03:33.420 --> 00:03:37.080
Clint: He is the best director who's done anime to live action style

00:03:37.120 --> 00:03:38.840
Gui: Yes
Clint: Um, like Shaolin Soccer

00:03:38.840 --> 00:03:39.480
Clint: Dude
Gui: Right

00:03:39.480 --> 00:03:39.980
Clint: Dude

00:03:46.000 --> 00:03:47.820
Gui: Just doing it non-stop and everybody's just running out

00:03:47.820 --> 00:03:49.460
Gui: "Ahhh... We're going to get hit... Ahhh..."

00:03:49.520 --> 00:03:51.000
Niko: Dude aim for the top hats

00:03:51.140 --> 00:03:52.880
[Laughter]

00:03:53.040 --> 00:03:59.780
Gui: So much style, so much, like, that... that soul that's in it makes it even more fun to watch

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:01.540
Niko: He's got the craziness in his eyes

00:04:01.540 --> 00:04:02.760
Niko: He's got that desperate... yeah

00:04:03.120 --> 00:04:08.000
Niko: He stomps with his foot when he hits at the same time and he holds it and everything just shakes because there's so much force behind it

00:04:08.240 --> 00:04:08.760
Clint: Yeah

00:04:09.020 --> 00:04:12.040
Niko: And like his chest is back, you know, it's like [Grunts]
Gui: Oh, man

00:04:12.640 --> 00:04:13.960
[Grunts]
Clint: Yeah

00:04:14.060 --> 00:04:15.580
Clint: It's so sick
Gui: It's so important

00:04:15.800 --> 00:04:16.500
[Fly buzzing]

00:04:16.500 --> 00:04:17.140
[Smack]

00:04:17.660 --> 00:04:19.900
Gui: Oh you.... mot-

00:04:20.240 --> 00:04:22.320
Niko: If anybody catches a fly on screen by the way

00:04:22.320 --> 00:04:24.380
Gui: I'm gonna... I'm ummm...

00:04:24.880 --> 00:04:27.120
Gui: By the end of this episode that that fly is mine

