00:10:41.900 --> 00:10:44.380
Niko: Let's just say they didn't have a lot of time on set

00:10:44.380 --> 00:10:48.360
Niko: You know, I would I would ascertain they maybe had a day or two to shoot this entire scene

00:10:48.460 --> 00:10:49.500
Niko: Gui? 
Gui: Yes?

00:10:49.500 --> 00:10:51.160
Niko: What would you do to make the scene better?

00:10:51.280 --> 00:10:57.160
Gui: I would get the shots that you need with your actors, your big points, and then I would use the wides that they have

00:10:57.200 --> 00:11:04.640
Gui: Where they're using the stunt performers and let that be the... the brandishing of the fight choreography and then cut in for the more visceral

00:11:04.720 --> 00:11:10.840
Gui: Intimate scenes that come on later on, but then it's up to the editor to make that come to fruition

00:11:11.040 --> 00:11:12.780
Gui: And I don't think it happened here

00:11:12.880 --> 00:11:17.340
Gui: And I get what they're trying to do because these are two very important characters to the story

00:11:17.360 --> 00:11:19.920
Gui: And they want to show them both being powerful

00:11:20.000 --> 00:11:24.300
Gui: But they're trying to get to the point of Brienne being able to win, her being a better fighter

00:11:24.480 --> 00:11:28.400
Gui: They could have played more to that and showed how she has to be smarter

00:11:28.640 --> 00:11:32.719
Gui: She has to be more strategic than just also being a brawler, or if they want her to just be a brawler

00:11:32.880 --> 00:11:34.880
Gui: Then they should just clash swords

00:11:35.040 --> 00:11:40.480
Gui: Somehow they both get disarmed and get right to the point of the nitty-gritty where they're punching and headbutting one another and then show

00:11:40.640 --> 00:11:43.599
Gui: Who has the best who, who has the most heart in that aspect

